.TH FL-VIDEO 1 "November 2026" "fldesktop 0.1.0" "fldesktop"
.SH NAME
fl-video \- video and audio player
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBfl-video\fR [\fB\-\-fullscreen\fR] [\fB\-\-software\fR] [\fIFILE\fR|\fIURL\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Plays video and audio files, playlists and network streams with \fBlibmpv\fR, so every format,
codec and subtitle type that \fBmpv\fR(1) supports works, including hardware decoding where
available. Several files make a playlist; files dropped on the window are added to it (with Ctrl
held, they replace it). Web addresses that \fByt-dlp\fR understands also play when it is installed.
Subtitle files next to a video (same name) are loaded automatically.
.PP
The position in each file is remembered when you quit and playback resumes there next time
(\fBResume Where I Left Off\fR in the menu turns this off). The screen stays on while a video plays.
.PP
Video is drawn with OpenGL; without a usable OpenGL driver fl-video falls back to mpv's software
renderer.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-f\fR, \fB\-\-fullscreen\fR
Start in full screen.
.TP
\fB\-\-software\fR
Use the software renderer (also \fBFLD_VIDEO_SW=1\fR).
.SH KEYS
.TP
\fBSpace\fR, \fBK\fR, click
Play / pause.
.TP
\fBLeft\fR / \fBRight\fR
Seek 5 seconds (with \fBShift\fR: 1 minute). \fB,\fR / \fB.\fR step one frame.
.TP
\fBUp\fR / \fBDown\fR, mouse wheel
Volume. \fBM\fR mutes.
.TP
\fBF\fR, \fBF11\fR, double-click
Full screen; \fBEscape\fR leaves it.
.TP
\fB[\fR / \fB]\fR, \fBBackspace\fR
Slower / faster, normal speed.
.TP
\fBN\fR / \fBP\fR
Next / previous playlist entry.
.TP
\fBJ\fR, \fBV\fR, \fB#\fR
Next subtitle track, show/hide subtitles, next audio track.
.TP
\fBS\fR
Screenshot into the Pictures folder.
.TP
\fBI\fR
Show file and codec information.
.TP
\fBCtrl+O\fR, \fBCtrl+U\fR, \fBCtrl+R\fR, \fBCtrl+Q\fR
Open files, open an address, repeat, quit.
.PP
Right-click (or the menu button) for audio, video and subtitle track selection, loading subtitle
files, speed, the playlist and the other options.
.SH FILES
.TP
\fI~/.config/fldesktop/video.ini\fR
Volume and the resume setting.
.TP
\fI~/.cache/fldesktop/watch_later/\fR
Remembered positions.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
\fBFLD_VIDEO_SW\fR
Set to 1 to always use the software renderer.
.TP
\fBFLD_VIDEO_DEBUG\fR
Print renderer and mpv log messages.
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBmpv\fR(1), \fBfl-files\fR(1)
